--------------------- CableDyn Input File ------------------------------------
CableDyn driver deck -- DYNAMIC polyester mooring, viscoelastic dynamic stiffness under waves
-- The same viscoelastic polyester rope as ve_polyester_catenary_mooring.dat, here marched in
-- time under a regular Airy wave (dtM/TMax set). This is where the DYNAMIC axial stiffness
-- matters: the static IC solves with Es, then each generalised-alpha step engages the
-- two-branch series-Kelvin dynamic branch (Ed, Bd) as the wave cycles the line tension -- the
-- physical distinction between a rope's slow-load and wave-frequency stiffness. Held fairlead
-- (the platform is stationary here); the wave field drives the line through Morison + FK.
